{"type":"message","id":"d80521cb","parentId":"17eca2e9","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:48:39.382Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The GET returns 401 Unauthorized now, but the POST returns 500 Internal Server Error with \"error code: 1101\". The 500 response body is just \"error code: 1101\" which is a Cloudflare Workers error (1101 = Worker exception).\n\nThe GET returned 401 earlier but returned data - that's confusing. Wait, actually looking again at the earlier calls - the GET returned data fine. Now it's returning 401. That's strange.\n\nActually wait - the GET /history returned 401 status code (with data?). No wait - \"curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\"\" showed 401, meaning the HTTP status code is 401. But the earlier GET calls returned actual data...\n\n\nSo the issue might be rate limiting - I'm getting 401 Unauthorized now, which could mean the key is being rejected or the service is blocking further requests. The GET worked earlier but now returns 401, which suggests the credentials might have changed or there's some kind of throttling happening","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":".\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-fc92af9f-b51f-4ada-a3b6-0805811e17b5","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}' \\\n  -w \"\\nHTTP_CODE:%{http_code}\" 2>&1 | grep -E \"(HTTP_CODE|error)\""},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"curl -s -X POST \\\"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"X-API-Key: echo-a…key\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\" \\\\\\n  -d '{\\\"threadId\\\":\\\"arbitration\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"test\\\"}' \\\\\\n  -w \\\"\\\\nHTTP_CODE:%